# CEO INDEX build law

OttoBot feels like a simple always-on chat. Underneath, CEOs and jobs are files.

## Chat surface

- Grok-simple chat: one composer, named bots, cards in the stream.
- Chat is UI only. Never send the full thread as the model prompt.
- Status / “what’s going on” reads INDEX (instance + aimed CEO). Tools off for Cos status.

## CEO from INDEX

- Each CEO owns `org/projects/<ceo>/INDEX.md` (Now / Last / Next / Blocker + law).
- Aiming a CEO loads that CEO’s INDEX / BRAIN / inbox — not another CEO’s.
- Host product CEO may still use id `openbot` on disk; user-facing name is OttoBot.

## Job packets

- Doing work builds a **job packet**: agent law + INDEX + BRAIN + ticket + this message + short RESULT hints.
- Thread JSON stays on disk for the human. Models get packets, not archives.

## Engines

- **OpenCode** — build / code / diffs (Builder, SupportBuilder).
- **Hermes Agent** — schedule, ops, research, long jobs, cron.
- **Board** — Cos status, routing, Accept UI. No third agent runtime.

## SupportBuilder

- Support is a CEO. Builder/SupportBuilder implements tickets as diffs.
- Support never Accepts, pushes, or posts live. Owner gates those.

## Multi-CEO isolation

- Separate work folders, Hermes homes, brains, and bus paths per CEO.
- Do not write one CEO’s job into another CEO’s tree.
- Shared keys/vault are instance-level; project state is not.

## Accept gates (human only)

- **Accept** required before: public post / publish, pay, delete (destructive), sign, merge/push when policy says so.
- Park send / publish / pay / delete on Needs-you cards. Never auto-approve those.
- Diff cards: Accept / Reject. Reject restores. No silent apply to production.

## Done

End jobs by updating the relevant INDEX (or BRAIN): Now / Last / Next / Blocker. Name the engine on the job card.
